{"_id":"696631973eeddc26d7c3a5f2","roadmapSlug":"ruby","nodeId":"mpsx0lr9ljlMEzuU5cZD6","description":"# Ruby Hashes\n\nHashes are collections of key-value pairs. Think of them like dictionaries, where each word (the key) has a definition (the value). Keys are unique within a hash, and they are used to quickly access their corresponding values. Hashes can store any type of data as keys and values, making them a versatile way to organize and retrieve information.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"class Hash","url":"https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/Hash.html","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7a9"},{"type":"article","title":"What is a Hash","url":"https://launchschool.com/books/ruby/read/hashes#whatisahash","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7aa"},{"type":"article","title":"Hashes - Odin Project","url":"https://www.theodinproject.com/lessons/ruby-hashes","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7ab"},{"type":"video","title":"Hashes | Ruby | Tutorial 14","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BtHKhsDUPwQ","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7ac"},{"type":"video","title":"Ruby Programming Tutorial - 31 - Hashes","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=imns9_XncQU","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd7ad"}],"createdAt":"2026-01-13T11:50:47.305Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:06:51.273Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ruby/content/mpsx0lr9ljlMEzuU5cZD6.md"}